cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository and the HIP-LLM
  paper whose reliability model it builds on.
title: >-
  HIP-HOPS-LLM: hierarchical imprecise reliability assessment and failure
  propagation for LLM-based agentic systems
abstract: >-
  A Python package that joins HiP-HOPS compositional safety analysis to the
  HIP-LLM hierarchical imprecise-probability reliability model. It extracts an
  architecture from a LangGraph application, synthesises static fault trees with
  minimal cut sets and a generated FMEA, calibrates their basic events from
  observed benchmark outcomes under an explicit operational profile, and converts
  the result into a Bayesian network for exact inference, diagnosis and
  visualisation.
type: software
authors:
